<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nationality question</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The nationality question was the problem of how to accommodate the many national groups within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-compromise-of-1867">1867 Compromise</a> satisfied the Hungarians but left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechs">Czechs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poles">Poles</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and others in subordinate positions. The resulting parliamentary obstruction and unrest made it the central governance challenge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>.</p></div>
